[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868614389","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106232#issuecomment-2868614389","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106232","id":2868614389,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6q-5T1","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T07:54:32Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T08:48:48Z","body":"This is because `Side` is a global enum, and your custom enum shadows it. In general, the intuitively expected order of name lookup should be: 1. local variables and constants, 2. class members, 3. global classes, functions, constants, and enums. But we have forced exceptions for global identifiers, since you can disambiguate class members like `MyClass.Side`, `self.load()`, but you can't reference global identifiers like `::Side`, `::load(\"res://test.tscn\")`.\n\nName shadowing is an error that is fairly easy to miss with dynamic typing, type inference, and in other cases. I would recommend avoiding name shadowing altogether, regardless of the state of affairs in GDScript. But I agree that the current behavior is probably buggy and should be reconsidered. However, we'll likely keep it for compatibility reasons, at least until Godot/GDScript introduces namespaces, which should help us solve naming conflicts.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868614389/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868632100","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106232#issuecomment-2868632100","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106232","id":2868632100,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6q-9ok","user":{"login":"BlackShift","id":5866818,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NjY4MTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5866818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlackShift","html_url":"https://github.com/BlackShift","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlackShift/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlackShift/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlackShift/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlackShift/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlackShift/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlackShift/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlackShift/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlackShift/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlackShift/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T08:33:09Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T08:33:09Z","body":"Thank you for the explanation, I completely missed that it was hiding a global, I thought I was going crazy! closing for now!",